CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding continues, especially along the Conejos River\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Conejos County...\n\n* WHEN...Until 115 AM MDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding will continue across low-lying and flood-prone\nlocations, especially along and near the Conejos River.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 506 PM MDT, Gauge reports indicate high stream flows\ncontinuing, although the Conejos River has crested at most\nlocations. Local law enforcement reports widespread standing and\nslow moving water around Manassa, with agricultural fields,\nwetlands and other low-lying areas inundated as well.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nManassa\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-27T01:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c1efb4a24b043b7472674533c0c4cf651f630555.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c1efb4a24b043b7472674533c0c4cf651f630555.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 25 at 9:00AM MDT until October 27 at 9:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall which occurred over\nthe last couple of days is expected or ongoing.\n\n* WHERE...Northeastern Conejos County in south central Colorado...\nSouthwestern Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 900 AM MDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding will occur in low-lying and flood-prone\nlocations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 852 AM MDT, flooding was occurring along the Rio Grande River\nin low lying and agricultural areas. This high water is due to\nall of the heavy rain which occurred over the last couple of\ndays.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include low lying\nareas in parts of Alamosa and parts of Conejos counties.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-27T09:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Con